--- body ---
## Context

During the raid-328/329 merge of PR #584 (2026-07-14), a plain
`erg-pr-merge 584` run died at its Step 1.5 existence guard with
"close-claimed ticket(s) 0329 are absent from tickets/ at branch tip" —
spuriously: `git ls-tree HEAD` showed the file present and the ticket ID was
correctly resolved. Cause: the rtk Bash hook rewrites `git ls-tree` output
(injects framing/truncation), corrupting the guard's grep over that output.
Re-running the helper under `bash -x` happened to bypass the rtk rewrite and
the guard passed cleanly; the merge then ran through normally.

This is the known "rtk rewrites git output" trap (memory
`feedback_rtk_rewrites_git_output`) landing inside a critical merge helper.
The standing workaround for machine-parsed git output is `rtk proxy git ...`,
but the helper's internals don't use it — so any invocation from a hooked
shell is exposed, and the `bash -x` escape is an accident, not a fix.

## Relevant files
- `scripts/erg-pr-merge` — Step 1.5 existence guard (`git ls-tree` + grep);
  audit the whole script for other machine-parsed git invocations
- Memory `feedback_rtk_rewrites_git_output` — the trap and the proxy idiom

## Actions
1. Audit erg-pr-merge for every git invocation whose stdout is parsed
   (ls-tree, rev-parse lists, diff --name-only, status --porcelain).
2. Make each robust under output-rewriting hooks: plumbing with explicit
   format flags parsed by exit code where possible, `rtk proxy git`
   otherwise — without hardcoding rtk (the script must still work where rtk
   is absent; probe or use an env-provided GIT wrapper).
3. Sweep sibling helpers in scripts/ that parse git output for the same
   exposure (worktree-salvage.sh, sync-local-main.sh at minimum).

## Test
- A test that runs the Step 1.5 guard logic with a wrapper that injects
  rtk-style framing lines into git stdout and asserts the guard still
  resolves presence correctly (RED against the current parsing).

## Invariants
- The guard must still fail loud when a close-claimed ticket is genuinely
  absent from the branch tip.
- `make check` passes.

## Sibling sweep disposition

Every helper that parses `git` stdout, with its disposition:

- `skills/merge/erg-pr-merge` — FIXED. Branch guard → `git symbolic-ref`
  (exit-code verdict); existence guard → compgen glob + `git cat-file -e`
  (no parsed stdout). Accepted limitation documented at the compgen site:
  it resolves the slug from the working tree, harmless because merge always
  runs on a clean PR-branch tip (working tree == HEAD).
- `scripts/sync-local-main.sh` — FIXED. Worktree-list parse hardened to
  porcelain record keys + NF==2 on the branch record.
- `scripts/worktree-salvage.sh` — CLEARED (no change). Already uses the
  `git symbolic-ref` exit-code idiom.
- `scripts/worktree-gc.sh` — FIXED. Same `git worktree list --porcelain`
  loop as sync-local-main.sh, and it is invoked via the Bash tool from
  `skills/molt` and `skills/roar`. The `branch refs/heads/*` arm now rejects
  a multi-token remainder (an appended framing banner like
  `branch refs/heads/main is stale`), which the old arm accepted as the
  branch name. Fail-closed rationale: even the old mis-parse could not cause
  a wrongful removal — a bad branch name just fails the later
  `for-each-ref` upstream-track lookup and the worktree is skipped — but the
  hardening makes the parse correct rather than merely safe. No dedicated
  suite exists (`tests/test_worktree_gc.sh` absent); per scope discipline no
  new suite was created — the hardening is defended by inspection and a
  RED-before/GREEN-after parser probe recorded in the commit.
- `scripts/guard-commit-on-main.sh` — CLEARED (no change). Uses
  `git branch --show-current` (a confirmed rewrite target) but it is a
  PreToolUse hook, spawned by the hook system and never via the Bash tool,
  so its internal git call is not subject to the outer Bash-tool rewrite.
  Out of scope.

## Exit criteria
- [x] erg-pr-merge's parsed-git call sites are hook-rewrite-proof
- [x] Regression test simulating rewritten git output is RED-before/GREEN-after
- [x] Sibling helper sweep done (fixed or explicitly cleared) — see disposition above
- [x] `make check` passes
